              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Assemble",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Blanch vermicelli in boiling water just until cooked — don't overcook, since it will continue absorbing sauce afterward.",
                "important": false
              },
              {
                "text": "While noodles are still warm, toss with a bit of the reserved chicken fat/oil to keep the strands from sticking and add aroma.",
                "important": false
              },
              {
                "text": "Pour the warm sauce over the noodles and toss to combine — using a spatula at first if too hot, then hands once cool enough, so the sauce is fully absorbed and the noodles turn tender.",
                "important": false
              },
              {
                "text": "Plate the noodles, then top with shredded chicken and crispy fried chicken skin.",
                "important": false
              }
            ]
          }
